WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:05.820
There was a man by the name of Alvin Roy.

2
00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:09.960
He had a little health spa down on Oklahoma Street [in Baton Rouge].

3
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.140
It’s no longer there, but I can show you where it was.

4
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:21.700
In the summer of ’58, he had Bob Pettit, Jim Taylor, Billy Cannon, Johnny Robinson,

5
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:28.680
Roy Winston who was still at Istrouma High School, and Norbert Roy who went on to Notre Dame from Istrouma High School.

6
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.020
All those guys played in the pros, you see.

7
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:43.140
Bob Pettit went from a skinny six [foot] nine [inch], 195-pound back-to-the-basket center at LSU to a power forward in the pros who weighed 225 pounds.

8
00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:53.420
If Alvin Roy’s not here—he’s one of the gurus of that business—I don’t think that LSU, you know, would have been as good because of,

9
00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.920
you know . . . Taylor, Cannon, all of them were lifting weights when nobody else was doing it.

10
00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.500
And he had been an Olympic weight lifting coach,

11
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:12.020
but he saw . . . I guess Cannon started lifting weights at Istrouma High School as a junior, his junior year.

12
00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:15.420
One year, Baton Rouge High kills Istrouma, okay?

13
00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:21.520
Istrouma starts lifting weights and the next year Istrouma kills Baton Rouge High.
